 35P  c  2008Wi09,2010WiZZ: A 230-MeV {+36}S beam was produced by the Argonne   
 35P 2c  Tandem Linac Accelerator System (ATLAS) with an intensity of 1.5 pnA on
 35P 3c  a 0.5 mg/cm{+2} {+208}Pb target and an intensity of 0.3 pnA on a 44    
 35P 4c  mg/cm{+2} {+208}Pb target. In the thin-target run, binary transfer     
 35P 5c  products were detected using a heavy-ion parallel-plate avalanche      
 35P 6c  counter (PPAC) array (CHICO) (Time resolution |?0.7 ns). The polar     
 35P 7c  angle covered was 12|'-85|' with respect to the beam. |g rays were     
 35P 8c  detected by Gammasphere consisting of 101 HPGe detectors with FWHM=2-10
 35P 9c  keV at E|g=1 MeV. Event-by-event Doppler shift correction was applied. 
 35P Ac  In the thick-target run, binary transfer products were stopped in the  
 35P Bc  target. |g rays were detected by Gammasphere consisting of 95 HPGe     
 35P Cc  detectors with FWHM=2-3 keV at E|g=1 MeV. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin.
 35P Dc  Deduced levels. Comparisons with shell-model calculations.             
 35P Ec  Branching-ratio limits were reported for predicted transitions to the  
 35P Fc  2~h|w bandheads in {+35}P and {+34}Si. An e-mail reply from Mathis     
 35P Gc  Wiedeking in April, 2010 (2010WiZZ) provides relative |g-ray           
 35P Hc  intensities, supplementing 2008Wi09.                                   
